f from `f966dfeb` to `c94d2da7` touches only `.pose/` records: indexes, the round-1 bundle and run records, and the start file. So the four round-1 findings are still there. All four are low severity and go forward as accepted follow-ups. Round 1 was refused only because `artifact-check` hadn't been run. I ran it this time and it exited 0, reporting 941 items, all of them repo-wide \"orphan\" warnings.\n\n## What I checked\n- **The fix** (`pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:783-794`, `:4468-4490`): the head is now picked as the first commit from `git rev-list --topo-order -n 1 <heads>`. That commit is always one of the input heads and no other input head descends from it, because any non-input commit is an ancestor of some input and would be listed later. The choice works whatever order the change sets are in, and a commit that isn't a full 40-character object id gives an empty result, which keeps the old head. A scope with a single head never calls Git, so spec scopes behave exactly as before.\n- **Sealed bundles keep their recorded head:** `reviewBundleSubject` is only called when a bundle is prepared (`review_bundle.go:522`) and from `review_structure.go:118`. Every check that uses the head compares the stored `Bundle.Payload.Subject.Head` and never recomputes it (`review_dispatch.go:543,1165,1534`, `review_run_provenance.go:755`, `review_run_continuity.go:390`, `delegation_handoff.go:312`). The bundle digest clears `Subject.Head`, `Base` and `ChangeSets` (`review_bundle.go:1963-1965`), so the new head doesn't change bundle identity.\n- **Head source:** `ResolvedHead` is read from the delivery-integrity index (`delivery_integrity.go:51`) and isn't validated before it reaches `rev-list` (R1-F1).\n- **Side note:** `artifact-check` resolved the change set `cs-9d0a5e7baf55` with head `2f525e14`. That commit is a descendant of the reviewed head, and it isn't an ancestor of `c94d2da7`. It's the commit that sealed this round's bundle. It's expected and isn't a defect.\n\n## Prior findings\n- **R1-F1:** not fixed. `review_bundle.go:4482` still has no `--` and doesn't validate the heads.\n- **R1-F2:** not fixed. When heads diverge, one tip is still picked without any warning.\n- **R1-F3:** not fixed. There is still no test that calls `reviewBundleSubject` with several change sets.\n- **R1-F4:** not fixed. Falling back to the last set's head still leaves no warning or reason in the bundle.\n\n## New finding\n- **N1 (low)**, `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:786`: `Subject.Base` still comes from the first change set by id, the same arbitrary choice this spec fixes for the head. The brief's displayed range (`review_brief.go:316`) and the design-delta range (`design_delta.go:184,269`) now pair the newest head with an arbitrary base. That range can leave out commits of members whose base is older.\n\n## Criteria\nAll criteria pass; the evidence and rationale for each are in the draft below.\n\n## Tools\n- **Passed:** `artifact-check` (run here) and both `validate` entries (from the sealed runs).\n- **`assess-design`:** cited from its sealed structure evidence. My own run was denied by the session's permission profile.\n- **Not used:** the other recommended tools, because the profile doesn't allow them.\n- **Deferred:** `review-check` and `closeout-check`, which can only run after the attestation.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"N1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\", \"line\": 786, \"summary\": \"Subject.Base is still taken from the first change set by id, the same arbitrary selection this spec fixes for the head; the brief range (review_brief.go:316) and the design-delta range (design_delta.go:184,269) now pair the newest head with an arbitrary base, which may exclude commits of members with older bases.\", \"action\": \"Select the base consistently with the head (e.g. the oldest base / merge-base of the sets) or document Base as advisory only, with a test over several change sets.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"}\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F1\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"git diff --stat f966dfeb..c94d2da7 touches only .pose/ records; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:4482 still passes unvalidated ResolvedHead values to rev-list without '--' (siblings at :1003, :1012, :969 terminate with '--').\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F2\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:783-794 unchanged since round 1: with divergent heads one maximal tip is chosen and no warning or blocker is appended.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F3\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_subject_head_newest_test.go only calls newestResolvedHead; no caller of reviewBundleSubject in tests (review_bundle_test.go:1123,1180, review_path_attribution_test.go:59, review_release_archive_test.go) builds several change sets with distinct heads; spec Known gaps confirms.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F4\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:4483-4485 returns \\\"\\\" on git error with no warning; caller at :791-794 silently keeps the last-by-id head; code unchanged since f966dfeb.\"}\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Diffed 6dbeddf2..c94d2da7 and f966dfeb..c94d2da7 (no code change since round 1); read reviewBundleSubject (review_bundle.go:704-850), newestResolvedHead (:4463-4490), reduceReviewBundleChangeSets (:1019), payload digest canonicalisation (:1957-1979); traced every non-test use of Subject.Head/Subject.Base (review_dispatch.go, review_run_provenance.go, review_run_continuity.go, delegation_handoff.go, review_rounds.go, federated_acceptance.go, design_delta.go, review_brief.go); checked ResolvedHead provenance (delivery_integrity.go:51) and captureGovernanceGit / governanceFullObjectID; read the new test, validation-matrix entry, changelog, start record and spec; ran pose artifact-check --strict (exit 0; 941 repo-wide orphan warnings only); checked ancestry of the change-set head artifact-check reported (2f525e14 descends from c94d2da7).\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-subject-head-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Verified: the topological first commit is always one of the input heads that no other input head descends from; sealed bundles are never recomputed (all Head consumers compare the stored value); the bundle digest excludes Head. Unresolved/accepted: divergent heads (R1-F2), silent fallback (R1-F4), no multi-set wiring test (R1-F3), governed files changed after the head (spec non-goal with recorded follow-up).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"The change adds one read-only, bounded git call through captureGovernanceGit inside bundle preparation; no shared state, goroutines or lifecycle changed.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\", \"rationale\": \"Bundle schema unchanged; Subject.Head is cleared from the payload digest (review_bundle.go:1965), so bundle identity is unaffected; only new multi-set bundles carry a different advisory head.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-subject-head-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Unknown head and single head return empty and fall back (test lines 29-34); output is accepted only if it is a full 40-hex object id. Missing '--'/pre-validation tracked as R1-F1 (low).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/milestone-review-proportional-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Milestone/roadmap bundle and dispatch suites pass on the sealed run; the dispatch consumes Subject.Head as the sealed commit (review_dispatch.go:543), which now contains every member's commits for linear histories.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"The chosen head is recorded in the bundle and printed in the brief range; the silent fallback lacks a reason (R1-F4, low, carried).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the bundle digest canonicalisation and every Head consumer; no CLI/MCP/file format change, sealed bundles keep their recorded head, spec scopes (single change set) are unchanged.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-subject-head-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Test covers three orderings, duplicate heads and an unknown head; read the code and found the selection sound for linear and divergent histories.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-f2cfbe5276c3bb83\", \"rationale\": \"Cause: subject.Head assigned per loop iteration over id-sorted sets (review_bundle.go:791) made the sealed commit arbitrary; D1 replaces it with the topological maximum, which does not depend on timestamps (same-second commits tie on date), so the sealed worktree (review_dispatch.go:543) contains every member's commits.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-subject-head-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Changelog entry (fixed, non-breaking) and spec Known gaps/Residual risks match the runtime behaviour I read; no operator docs describe the head choice.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Removes the 'sealed checkout inputs differ'/'no sealed review bundle' failures caused by an old sealed commit; residual silent fallback is R1-F4 (low).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-subject-head-integration\", \"rationale\": \"R1 tested directly; R2 wiring verified by reading review_bundle.go:783-794, test gap tracked as R1-F3 (low).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-subject-head-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Compared the diff with the spec artifacts list: only review_bundle.go, the new test, the matrix entry, start and changelog changed, matching the declared artifacts; Base selection left untouched (N1).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the new git invocation: arguments come from the governed delivery-integrity index, run via gitCommand with no shell; rev-list has no write-capable options and the output is validated as a full object id. Hardening (pre-validation and '--') tracked as R1-F1 (low).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-f2cfbe5276c3bb83\", \"rationale\": \"Compared with sorting by commit date (rejected in D1 because same-second commits tie); one helper and a single git call, skipped for single-head scopes; no speculative extension. The choice would be invalidated if the sets' heads routinely diverge (merge workflows), see R1-F2.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-subject-head-is-the-newest --strict\", \"rationale\": \"Exit 0; change_set cs-9d0a5e7baf55, claims=6, observed=22, findings=941, all '[!] warning orphan' repo-wide provenance warnings, none for this scope's paths.\"},\n    {\"